    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "SFO\nSECOND LEVEL PLAN\nGROUND LEVEL PLAN\nSAN\nFRANCISCO\nINTERNATIONAL\nAIRPORT\nNORTH TERMINAL\n• The major addition to the terminal ring is the North Terminal.\nThis three story structure will be 1050 feet long and contain\n•350,000 sq. ft., plus a 140,000 sq. ft. basement in which\nmechanical rooms, storage and baggage input are located.\nThe terminal serves 9 frontal aircraft gates and three new\nrotundas accommodating 18 additional aircraft gates.\nThe second level provides baggage check-in and ticket\ncounter space for four major airlines, a large cocktail lounge\nand food service facility, newsstand, gift shop, bank and\nother concessions.\nTwo bridges and two tunnels connect the terminal to the\nparking structure. The open planning of the terminal allows\nthrough circulation to the frontal holding rooms and to the\nconnectors leading to the rotundas.\nThe ground level provides baggage return for arriving passengers\nat 14 claim devices, plus airline and concession support facilities.\nPassengers arriving from the rotunda and frontal gates descend to\nthe ground level by escalators and are directed to the claim device\nfor their flight by electronic signs. The passenger then proceeds\nto the lower road curb or to the garage by tunnels.\nThe exterior finish will be precast concrete panels with exposed\ngrey granite aggregate. The grey glass will be set in black\naluminum frames."
    ],
